Subject: [PATCH] Picture pacer: a provider that hands its pictures over on a schedule of its own

Transformers' native renderer (TODO N9, docs/TODO.md 95) hands each picture over at its frame's moment
plus a steady delay, so that the pictures reach the screen evenly. The window used to show a provided
picture only at a VBlank, whichever was newest then: its place among the VBlanks moved with the render
thread's and the GPU's times (a picture up one VBlank, two or three). With a pacer set
(ps2_host_display::setPicturePacer) the window waits on the pacer instead of the VBlanks and draws the
moment one is handed over; -1 from the pacer (no provided picture now: a movie, a screen it does not
draw) falls back to the VBlanks. The FPS counter then counts the pictures the window shows.
---
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_display.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_display.h
@@ -109,6 +109,19 @@
     using PictureProvider = bool (*)(unsigned int &texture, int &width, int &height);
     void setPictureProvider(PictureProvider provider);
     PictureProvider pictureProvider();
+    // When the provider's pictures are shown (a game whose renderer paces its own pictures - each
+    // handed over at the moment it is to be on the screen, so that they reach it evenly): `wait`
+    // replaces the window's wait for a VBlank - it returns 1 when a new picture is to be shown now,
+    // 0 when none came by `until`, -1 when the provider has none now (the VBlanks' pictures then, as
+    // without a pacer: a movie, a screen it does not draw). `presented`, if any, is told when the
+    // window has presented the picture. Null (the default): the window shows a picture each VBlank.
+    struct PicturePacer
+    {
+        int (*wait)(std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point until) = nullptr;
+        void (*presented)() = nullptr;
+    };
+    void setPicturePacer(PicturePacer pacer);
+    PicturePacer picturePacer();
 
     // The emulated drawing switched off (a native renderer drawing the frame itself): the GS draws
     // no primitive, while everything the EE can observe goes on - DMA, VIF1 and VU1 (its programs
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_display.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_display.cpp
@@ -684,6 +684,26 @@
 
     namespace
     {
+        std::atomic<int (*)(Clock::time_point)> g_pacerWait{nullptr};
+        std::atomic<void (*)()> g_pacerPresented{nullptr};
+    }
+
+    void setPicturePacer(PicturePacer pacer)
+    {
+        g_pacerPresented.store(pacer.presented, std::memory_order_release);
+        g_pacerWait.store(pacer.wait, std::memory_order_release);
+    }
+
+    PicturePacer picturePacer()
+    {
+        PicturePacer pacer;
+        pacer.wait = g_pacerWait.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+        pacer.presented = g_pacerPresented.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+        return pacer;
+    }
+
+    namespace
+    {
         std::atomic<bool> g_emulatedDrawing{true};
     }
 
